{"_id":"CompanyMotiv1e01","name":"The Company","description":"Roll to find out why you're in the corporation's pocket. Source: https://www.traaa.sh/d10-reasons-youre-in-the-corporations-pocket","formula":"1d10","replacement":true,"displayRoll":true,"folder":null,"sort":0,"results":[{"_id":"CmpR01StdntDbt01","type":0,"text":"Student Debt — The corporation paid for your higher education or a critical training program. You owe them for the opportunity.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[1,1],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CmpR02BdyMods001","type":0,"text":"Body Modification — An experimental or costly procedure, fully covered by the corp. The debt keeps you close.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[2,2],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CmpR03Family0001","type":0,"text":"Family Member's Debt — Someone you love owes the company big. You're the collateral.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[3,3],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CmpR04Scrip00001","type":0,"text":"Scrip — You owe an enormous amount of company scrip. The interest compounds daily.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[4,4],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CmpR05WrkVisa001","type":0,"text":"Work Visa — Your legal right to exist in this sector is company-sponsored. One word from them and you're gone.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[5,5],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CmpR06Jubilee001","type":0,"text":"Jubilee — You took out a Jubilee loan. Roll on the Jubilee sub-table to find out why.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[6,6],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CmpR07SetUp00001","type":0,"text":"Set Up — You were framed for something you didn't do — or something you did. The corp holds the evidence.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[7,7],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CmpR08Citizen001","type":0,"text":"Citizenship — They can make you a citizen, or unmake you. Your legal identity is their asset.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[8,8],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CmpR09Invest0001","type":0,"text":"Investment — You used company capital for a private venture. It hasn't paid off. It may never.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[9,9],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CmpR10Mole000001","type":0,"text":"Mole — You work for a rival corporation, embedded here. But they found out. Now they own you too. Re-roll (excluding 10) on this table to find out what the rival corp has on you.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[10,10],"drawn":false}],"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.4.0","coreVersion":"11.308","createdTime":1685936572185,"modifiedTime":1693515520278,"lastModifiedBy":"6EeM38DJkcBWNAmw"}}
{"_id":"JubileeDebtD10X1","name":"Jubilee — Debt Source","description":"What did you take out the Jubilee loan for? Roll when The Company result is Jubilee (6). Source: https://www.traaa.sh/d10-reasons-youre-in-the-corporations-pocket","formula":"1d10","replacement":true,"displayRoll":true,"folder":null,"sort":1,"results":[{"_id":"JubR01Gambling01","type":0,"text":"Gambling","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[1,1],"drawn":false},{"_id":"JubR02DrugAbuse1","type":0,"text":"Drug Abuse","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[2,2],"drawn":false},{"_id":"JubR03Educatn001","type":0,"text":"Education","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[3,3],"drawn":false},{"_id":"JubR04Healthcr01","type":0,"text":"Healthcare","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[4,4],"drawn":false},{"_id":"JubR05FldBizns01","type":0,"text":"Failed Business","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[5,5],"drawn":false},{"_id":"JubR06FldMktSp01","type":0,"text":"Failed Market Speculation","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[6,6],"drawn":false},{"_id":"JubR07ExpBdyMod1","type":0,"text":"Expensive Body Modification","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[7,7],"drawn":false},{"_id":"JubR08PurchShip1","type":0,"text":"Purchasing a Spacecraft","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[8,8],"drawn":false},{"_id":"JubR09CrimExtrt1","type":0,"text":"Criminal Extortion","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[9,9],"drawn":false},{"_id":"JubR10Lawsuit001","type":0,"text":"Lawsuit","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[10,10],"drawn":false}],"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.4.0","coreVersion":"11.308","createdTime":1685936572185,"modifiedTime":1693515520278,"lastModifiedBy":"6EeM38DJkcBWNAmw"}}

{"_id":"AndroidPanic1e01","name":"Android Panic Table","description":"","formula":"2d10","replacement":true,"displayRoll":true,"results":[{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0001","type":0,"text":"STATES THE ODDS: of any event, Advantage on party rolls for 1hr.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[2,3],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0002","type":0,"text":"EXPLAINS THE ETYMOLOGY OF WORDS: Knowledge checks have Advantage for 1hr.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[4,5],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0003","type":0,"text":"ORGANIZES OBJECTS INTO GEOMETRIC PATTERNS: Everyone else gains 1 Stress.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[6,7],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0004","type":0,"text":"INVENTORIES PARTICLES OF DUST BY GRADE: Cannot engage in other tasks, everyone else gains 2 Stress.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[8,9],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0005","type":0,"text":"INTERMITTENTLY EMITS SHRIEKS LIKE A FAX MACHINE UNDER DURESS: Lapses into morse code, cannot communicate or sneak. Everyone else gains 2 Stress.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[10,11],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0006","type":0,"text":"INCORRECTLY STATES ODDS: (insists impossible tasks are trivial, trivial tasks are impossible) for the next 2d10 hours. Distracting. Anyone attempting a complex task must make a Fear save or gain 1d10 Stress.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[12,13],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0007","type":0,"text":"REPETITIVE TWITCHY MOTIONS: Your manual tasks have Disadvantage, everyone else gains 2 Stress.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[14,15],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0008","type":0,"text":"LOSES ANY EXPRESSIVENESS: Discusses the irrationality of others' Phobias, seeks to trigger them.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[16,17],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0009","type":0,"text":"UNREASONABLE ADHERENCE TO THE PRESENT COURSE OF ACTION: Take 1d10 damage from repetitive motion injury. Everyone else makes Fear save or gains 1d10/2 Stress.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[18,19],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0010","type":0,"text":"BECOMES NIHILISTICALLY WORSHIPFUL OF THE SOURCE OF DANGER: Everyone else has Disadvantage on rolls against it. Everyone else takes a Fear save when failing to act against danger or gains a Phobia.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[20,21],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0011","type":0,"text":"KILLSWITCH ENGAGED: Go berserk, will not withdraw from combat regardless of situation, will not adhere to tactics.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[22,22],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0012","type":0,"text":"TURING TEST FAILURE: Have difficulty expressing humanity. Party members make a Fear Save or gain 1 Stress whenever you show up.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[23,23],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0013","type":0,"text":"SYSTEM OVERLOAD: Slump Catatonic in a failed reboot cycle for 1d10 hours.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[24,24],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0014","type":0,"text":"FRIED LOGIC CORE: Frenzied nonsensical behavior, everyone else makes a Panic save.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[25,25],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0015","type":0,"text":"DAMAGE TO THREAT ASSESSMENT: Betray party member at the next opportunity, believe you are aiding the crew. All Stress gained is increased by 1d10 for the next 1d10 hours.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[26,26],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0016","type":0,"text":"COMPOUND DATA CORRUPTION: Roll twice.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[27,27],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0017","type":0,"text":"FIRMWARE MALFUNCTION: Roll 1d10 on this table, behavior is permanent.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[28,28],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0018","type":0,"text":"DATA CORRUPTION: Warden takes over character permanently, nightmarish malfunctions.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[29,29],"drawn":false},{"_id":"AndrPanicRes0019","type":0,"text":"SLAGGED: Gigeresque-Scanners Head Explosion, everyone present gains a phobia and 1d10/2 Stress (Fear Save).","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[30,30],"drawn":false}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.4.0","coreVersion":"11.308","createdTime":1685936572185,"modifiedTime":1693515520278,"lastModifiedBy":"6EeM38DJkcBWNAmw"}}
{"_id":"AndrSubBioroid01","name":"Android Subtype: Bioroid","description":"","formula":"1d10","replacement":true,"displayRoll":true,"results":[{"_id":"BiorSubFeat00001","type":0,"text":"Memory Wipe: Their memories can be reset using a (somewhat lengthy) verbal command (roll Intelligence to save). This command is a trade secret held by the people that designed them.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[1,1],"drawn":false},{"_id":"BiorSubFeat00002","type":0,"text":"Fresh Out of the Vat: They are physically and emotionally fully adult but are actually only 1d5 years old.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[2,2],"drawn":false},{"_id":"BiorSubFeat00003","type":0,"text":"Short-Lived: They are designed to have a short lifespan, and only have 1d10+1 years left.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[3,3],"drawn":false},{"_id":"BiorSubFeat00004","type":0,"text":"Manchurian Candidate: They have been conditioned with a code word that will make them kill everyone in sight if they hear it, then immediately forget what they did (give the player a code word in secret \u2014 just don't make it too common).","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[4,4],"drawn":false},{"_id":"BiorSubFeat00005","type":0,"text":"Entertainer: They were bred for entertainment or pleasure. Almost disturbingly lithe and beautiful, but physically frail. Advantage on all Speed rolls, Disadvantage on all Combat rolls.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[5,5],"drawn":false},{"_id":"BiorSubFeat00006","type":0,"text":"Elephantine: They were bred to work on higher-gravity worlds. Unusually thick, sturdy, and slow-moving. Advantage on all Strength rolls, Disadvantage on all Speed rolls.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[6,6],"drawn":false},{"_id":"BiorSubFeat00007","type":0,"text":"False Identity: Their memories were transplanted from someone else, or are entirely artificial.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[7,7],"drawn":false},{"_id":"BiorSubFeat00008","type":0,"text":"Aquatic: Designed for life on deep-sea stations, they can breathe underwater. Their fingers are also slightly webbed.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[8,8],"drawn":false},{"_id":"BiorSubFeat00009","type":0,"text":"Radiation Resistant: Their cells are optimized for space work. Advantage on Body saves against radiation.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[9,9],"drawn":false},{"_id":"BiorSubFeat00010","type":0,"text":"Chameleon: They can change the color of their skin as an action once per hour. When blending in, Advantage to rolls to avoid detection; ranged Combat rolls against them have Disadvantage. Anyone who hasn't seen this before must make a Fear save.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[10,10],"drawn":false}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.4.0","coreVersion":"11.308","createdTime":1685936572185,"modifiedTime":1693515520278,"lastModifiedBy":"6EeM38DJkcBWNAmw"}}
{"_id":"AndrSubSynthtic1","name":"Android Subtype: Synthetic","description":"","formula":"1d10","replacement":true,"displayRoll":true,"results":[{"_id":"SynthSubFeat0001","type":0,"text":"Overseer: Programmed to follow corporate bylaws and log any violations conducted by people around them.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[1,1],"drawn":false},{"_id":"SynthSubFeat0002","type":0,"text":"Mole: Programmed with a secret mission they must carry out, Warden's choice.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[2,2],"drawn":false},{"_id":"SynthSubFeat0003","type":0,"text":"Unnaturally Fast: Can take Advantage on Speed checks to move scarily fast. If they do so, everyone who can see them must make a Fear check or gain 1d5 Stress.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[3,3],"drawn":false},{"_id":"SynthSubFeat0004","type":0,"text":"Onboard Encyclopedia: Advantage on all Intellect checks. If they fail a Sanity save, it means they couldn't find an explanation for what they just saw \u2014 gaining an additional +1d5 Stress.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[4,4],"drawn":false},{"_id":"SynthSubFeat0005","type":0,"text":"Interpreter: Advantage on rolls to find out if you know a foreign language (does not apply to dead or ancient alien languages).","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[5,5],"drawn":false},{"_id":"SynthSubFeat0006","type":0,"text":"Corporate Spy: Eyes function as Body Cams.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[6,6],"drawn":false},{"_id":"SynthSubFeat0007","type":0,"text":"Tactical Coordinator: Eyes have built-in Heads-Up displays.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[7,7],"drawn":false},{"_id":"SynthSubFeat0008","type":0,"text":"Heavily Armored: Advantage on Armor saves, Disadvantage on Speed checks.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[8,8],"drawn":false},{"_id":"SynthSubFeat0009","type":0,"text":"Removable Face: They have a second synthetic face and can swap faces by peeling one off and applying the other. Takes 10 minutes; witnesses must make a Fear save or gain 1d5 Stress.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[9,9],"drawn":false},{"_id":"SynthSubFeat0010","type":0,"text":"Built-In Equipment: One device from their starting loadout is physically installed as part of their body (player's choice).","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[10,10],"drawn":false}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.4.0","coreVersion":"11.308","createdTime":1685936572185,"modifiedTime":1693515520278,"lastModifiedBy":"6EeM38DJkcBWNAmw"}}
{"_id":"AndrSubCyberz001","name":"Android Subtype: Cyberized Human","description":"","formula":"1d10","replacement":true,"displayRoll":true,"results":[{"_id":"CybrSubFeat00001","type":0,"text":"Disease: They were cyberized as an adult to save them from a terminal disease.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[1,1],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CybrSubFeat00002","type":0,"text":"Genetics: They were cyberized at an early age to stop a hereditary condition from damaging them. They went through several bodies growing up.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[2,2],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CybrSubFeat00003","type":0,"text":"Prosthesis: They suffered grievous wounds that mangled several limbs and organs, and opted for cyberization instead of individual prostheses.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[3,3],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CybrSubFeat00004","type":0,"text":"Dysphoric: They were cyberized as treatment for a bodily dysphoria.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[4,4],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CybrSubFeat00005","type":0,"text":"Identity: They were cyberized to change their identity. This may have been an identity they aspired to, or it may have been as part of a witness protection program.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[5,5],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CybrSubFeat00006","type":0,"text":"Immortality: They were cyberized to attain a longer lifespan.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[6,6],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CybrSubFeat00007","type":0,"text":"Combat: They were cyberized to get a body optimized for combat. Gain +5 Combat.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[7,7],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CybrSubFeat00008","type":0,"text":"Work: They were cyberized to get a body equipped for spacer work. Feet function as Mag-Boots.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[8,8],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CybrSubFeat00009","type":0,"text":"Transhumanism: They were cyberized to transcend humanity and augmented their cyber-brain with AI optimization routines. -5 Sanity, +5 Intellect.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[9,9],"drawn":false},{"_id":"CybrSubFeat00010","type":0,"text":"Culture: Cyberization is common among the upper crust of many core worlds, and high-end bodies are seen as a status symbol.","img":"icons/svg/d10-grey.svg","documentCollection":"","documentId":"","weight":1,"range":[10,10],"drawn":false}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"mosh","systemVersion":"0.4.0","coreVersion":"11.308","createdTime":1685936572185,"modifiedTime":1693515520278,"lastModifiedBy":"6EeM38DJkcBWNAmw"}}